==English==
{{Wikiquote}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ar|مُجَاهِد}}, {{ar-active participle|lc=1|nocat=1}} of {{m|ar|جَاهَدَ||to strive in the cause of God}} (verbal noun: {{m|ar|جِهَاد||to strive in the cause of God as a religious duty}}), from the root {{ar-root|ج|ه|د|nocat=1}}. {{root|en|ar|ج ه د}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/mʊˈdʒɑːhɪd/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|mujahideen|mujahidin|s}}

# {{lb|en|Islam}} A Muslim engaging in [[jihad]], especially armed jihad; a [[jihadist]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|jihadist}}, {{l|en|jihadi}}

